AB  - The emergence of the Internet of Things (IoT) has profoundly transformed the way companies manage their business processes by providing real-time information from a variety of wireless devices. However, integrating Internet of Things information into business processes presents major challenges due to the diversity and volume of the data. Our contributions were aimed at improving business process management in the context of the Internet of Things. In this particular context, a major obstacle to autonomous business process detection is the lack of modeling concepts that characterize Internet of Things components as part of a business process model. In previous studies, we investigated and compared process modeling in intelligent environments based on process mining to provide a framework for discovering business process models from sensor data. The usefulness of this method is associated with process modeling, which does not include IoT components such as devices and output data. In this work, we proposed an extended BPMN ontology model for the Internet of Things, which served as the basis for a semantic framework.
