AB  - This study investigates the impact of Requirements with Logs (RWL), a standardized software design approach, on the efficiency of Business Process Automation (BPA) software development. Conducted in a technology institute responsible for automating processes in a global organization, the research focuses on a development team creating BPA software for automating Latin requirements integration in Android releases. The study evaluates the effectiveness of RWL by analyzing Issue Resolution Time (IRT) and Bug Resolution Time (BRT) metrics. Data collected over a five-month period revealed significant improvements in development efficiency. Compared to previous projects without RWL, the team achieved a 49.88% reduction in IRT (from 16.68 to 8.36 hours) and a 50.40% reduction in BRT (from 20.14 to 9.99 hours). These results suggest that RWL enhances BPA software development efficiency, demonstrating its potential to streamline operations and reduce development bottlenecks in complex, process-driven environments.
