AB  - Addressing the challenge of combinatorial explosion in workflow path recommendation caused by complex parallel structures, which leads to exponential growth of the feasible path space and makes it difficult for traditional methods to efficiently locate high-quality paths, this paper proposes an event log-enhanced Direction-Aware Ant Colony Optimization algorithm. This method automatically extracts and quantifies dependency strength and execution priority between tasks from historical event logs using process mining techniques, constructing a direction factor integrated with business semantics to guide the ant colony algorithm in conducting efficient searches within the vast path space. ELOBACO effectively mitigates the combinatorial explosion problem, rapidly converging towards mainstream paths. It achieves a path coverage rate of 85.2%, a compliance rate of 94.3%, and demonstrates significantly superior convergence speed compared to baseline algorithms.
