AB  - With the rapid development of computer technology, the Internet age has become the mainstream. The problem of information security has become very serious. Especially, the security of database system, the protection of data and the prevention of illegal destruction have become the focus of social attention. The security of software is the foundation of computer security and communication security. No matter how good firewall, intrusion detection and anti-virus software is, if the security of the software itself can't be guaranteed, then it can't improve the security at all. The fundamental reason is that the most important problem of computer security is the defect of computer software. Blocking the attacker's attack from the outside is always a temporary solution but not a permanent cure, and the core part of the problem is not grasped, so the effect is minimal. Therefore, how to detect the vulnerabilities in the software system in advance is an urgent problem to be solved in the field of software security. In this paper, we propose a COQ based formal method and proof system to verify the above three types of operations against the nonstandard operations that threaten software security, such as array overrun, null pointer reference and buffer overflow. The results show that the method proposed in this paper effectively verifies three types of problems in software security, and lays a foundation for the application of formal methods in software security verification.
