AB  - We present a particle-based fluid simulation method that integrates a Monte Carlo pressure solver into the Smoothed Particle Hydrodynamics (SPH) framework. The Monte Carlo solver efficiently handles with complex boundary geometries and benefits from GPU ray tracing. While previous work has primarily employed Monte Carlo solvers within a semi-Lagrangian framework, our approach is the first to incorporate such a solver into a pure Lagrangian (SPH) framework. Our method adapts sampling strategies according to the particle distribution and maps neighbor search to ray tracing, allowing for seamless integration within SPH. We demonstrate that our method’s simplicity and parallelizability make it a promising alternative for simulating incompressible flows with complex solid boundaries.
