TI  - DRLBPSS: Deep Reinforcement Learning-Based Parallel Strategy Search with Inference Acceleration for Large Language Models
AU  - Wen, Ruiming
AU  - Xiong, Buyao
AU  - Ou, Jie
AU  - ILager, Shashikant
AU  - Tian, Wenhong
PY  - 2025
AB  - The exponential growth of large language model parameters poses significant challenges for distributed training efficiency. Traditional manual tuning of parallel strategies suffers from vast search spaces and poor hardware adaptability, while existing automated methods struggle to balance search efficiency and strategy optimality. This paper presents DRLBPSS (Deep Reinforcement Learning-based Parallel Strategy Search), a novel algorithm that automates the search for optimal distributed parallel strategies in the MindSpore framework. DRLBPSS employs attention-based dynamic pruning to transform embeddings into distributed parallel strategies, effectively addressing the search space explosion problem. Furthermore, we introduce Lookup Attention, a dynamic sparse attention mechanism that accelerates inference by converting global attention computation into efficient vector retrieval. Experimental results on BERT, GPT, and LLaMA2 models demonstrate that DRLBPSS achieves 1.1–$1.3 \times$ improvement in training efficiency compared to traditional uniform partitioning strategies and 4-10x speedup in search time compared to state-of-the-art algorithms like Alpa and AMP. The proposed Lookup Attention reduces inference time by approximately 66 %, validating the effectiveness of our approach in both strategy search and inference acceleration.
