AB  - Variational inference (VI) based image registration estimates the variational posterior of the displacement vector field (DVF), providing uncertainty information and demonstrating potential for generalization performance. This paper proposes a probabilistic image registration framework utilizing self-normalized importance sampling (NISAE) of the posterior to achieve a tighter evidence lower bound (ELBO), and control variates are introduced to reduce the variance of the gradient estimator for the ELBO. We theoretically prove that the gradient estimator of the ELBO improves the signal-to-noise ratio (SNR) as the number of samples increases. The variance reduction ensures the training converges faster and stable. Our NISAE is a general framework that can be combined with any VIbased registration model to improve its performance. Extensive experiments on public cardiac image datasets demonstrate that our NISAE achieves enhanced performance on small training sets and cross-domain datasets compared to state-of-the-art probabilistic registration models.
