AB  - To achieve optimal control of the parafoil precision airdrop system in the terminal homing stage, we propose in the present work a real-time control method based on the deep neural network (DNN). This control method combines the Gaussian pseudo-spectral method (GPM) to generate an optimal trajectory with a DNN capable of functional learning. The terminal homing process of the parafoil system was simplified into an optimal control problem which was then solved by the GPM. The results were used as training samples to establish a reasonable functional relationship between state variables and control variables in the DNN model. The DNN controller was obtained by embedding the trained DNN model into the real-time control process, with numerical simulation experiments carried out on a small parafoil system to verify the real-time control ability and robustness of our proposed method.
