AB  - We study the secrecy outage performance of a dual-hop multiple relay decode-and-forward (DF) cognitive relay network under the interference constraints in this paper, where all relays and the destination are equipped with K antennas. All channels we considered in the proposed system experience the Nakagami-m fading, and the selection combining technique is employed at the antennas of all the main link receiving nodes. An eavesdropper with single antenna could wiretap the information at each hop, and the transmit power at the main link is limited by the interference constraints of the primary user receiver. We derive the exact system secrecy outage probability to evaluate the system secrecy performance, and the Monte-Carlo simulation results are also given to validate the veracity of the numerical analytical results.
