AB  - We study the multiple relay cognitive relay network under the interference constraints of primary user in this paper, and the secrecy performance of the secondary network with the decode-and-forward (DF) relaying protocol is analysed. Secrecy outage probabilities in accurate and asymptotic forms and the probabilities of nonzero secrecy capacity are derived respectively to evaluate our proposed system secrecy performance, when the conventional relay selection is employed to select the best relay. There exists direct links, and all channels we considered are Rayleigh fading channels. In the high main-to-eavesdropper ratio environment, we can realize that the system diversity order equals to K + 1 from asymptotic secrecy outage probabilities, where K represents the quantity of relays. We also present Monte Carlo simulation results, which can validate the accuracy of analytic results.
