AB  - AI model compatibility is one of the key focuses in the pilot testing of AI applications. To address the challenge of compatibility evaluation in multi-model AI systems, this paper proposes the CompScore framework. This framework leverages Coupled Markov Chains (CMC) to simulate and quantify the dynamic interactions between models. Each model is abstracted as a Markov chain, and their interactions are modeled via a coupling kernel. We introduce a comprehensive "Compatibility Score" (CompScore) that integrates four key dimensions: synergy, stability, task performance, and efficiency. Experiments show that CompScore's predictions highly correlate with theoretical ground truth in controlled settings and with human evaluations in multi- agent reinforcement learning (MARL) tasks (Spearman's ρ = 0.89), providing an effective and interpretable scientific basis for the a priori assessment of model combinations.
