TY  - CPAPER
TI  - Hierarchical urban land use and its 3D application
AU  - Chen, Zhangwu
AU  - Ro, Bin
AU  - Zhu, Zhongguan
PY  - 2021
AB  - Urban land use information is of great significance for many applications based on Geographic Information System (GIS), such as autonomous driving. There are big differences in people, objects, and their movement patterns in different land-use types, which is a big challenge for autonomous driving. And the existing virtual autonomous driving simulation rarely considers the transition between different land types. Traditional land-use planning methods are mostly based on simulation modeling of agents. It simulates the early urban development process in reality and spreads from the center of the topographic map to the outside, which usually takes a long time. To improve the efficiency of land use simulation, this paper proposes a spatial adaptive parallel simulation algorithm: Based on the value of land development, the land area is adaptively divided based on the quad-tree structure, and perform agent-based urban development simulation operations on the divided sub-areas. After the simulation is completed, the land-use type of the divided sub-areas is determined according to the “voting” rule. Finally, the corresponding 3D city model is constructed according to the land-use type, and the 3D buildings of each area and their distribution are automatically generated according to the land-use type using a procedural method. The experimental results prove the effectiveness of the method in this paper, and the 3D virtual city constructed according to this method can be used in urban construction, games, movie production, and autonomous driving simulation.
