AB  - Network slicing technology partitions physical resources into multiple virtual end-to-end slices to meet the diverse and heterogeneous service requirements of users. Therefore, achieving fair and efficient dynamic resource allocation has become the key to optimizing network performance. Deep Reinforcement Learning (DRL) has been demonstrated as a feasible solution for excavating the dynamic characteristics of network slices to enable dynamic resource allocation. However, the complexity of the network environment and the vast amount of data lead to low learning efficiency of the agent. Furthermore, in multi-slice deployment scenarios, applying DRL techniques easily induces the curse of dimensionality problem within the large-scale action space. To address this challenge, this paper proposes a Transfer Deep Deterministic Policy Gradient (Transfer-DDPG) algorithm. It accelerates the learning speed of the agent by introducing prior knowledge of optimal action selection and achieves efficient handling of the large-scale action space in multislice scenarios by reconstructing the network architecture and the policy learning process. Simulation results demonstrate that the proposed algorithm can efficiently achieve resource allocation in multi-slice environments and significantly improves the learning efficiency of the agent.
