PY  - 2025
AB  - Time series data often exhibit complex characteristics, such as multiple seasonal patterns and multivariate interdependencies, which, when effectively modeled, can significantly enhance forecasting accuracy and anomaly detection capabilities. However, existing models cannot simultaneously capture multiple seasonalities and the interdependencies between variables, limiting their predictive and anomaly detection potential. This paper proposes a new multi-seasonal multivariate Seasonal Autoregressive Integrated Moving Average (SARIMA) model to address these shortcomings and significantly improve anomaly detection accuracy in multivariate multi-seasonal time series data while maintaining practical runtimes. Our experimental results demonstrate superior performance when compared to an existing multivariate SARIMA model, and the common Vector Autoregressive Moving Average model (VARMA), as well as seasonal VARMA variations.
