TY  - CPAPER
TI  - Predicting the Unpredictable: Using Monte Carlo Simulation to Predict
Project Completion Date
AU  - Colucci, Lucas
AU  - Albino, Raphael
PY  - 2017
AB  - If you work with software development you will probably face two
important, but not always convergent, aspects: scope and delivery
cadence. The process of aligning the expectations of product increment
and team throughput is usually arduous but, when this happens, it
improves the chances of project success. Stakeholders frequently want
the project done faster than it is possible for us to do it. And then,
when they ask the date on which we will finish the work, we never have
the right answer. In the last two years, while working with different
projects at Plataformatec, we have been trying to solve that problem in
many different ways: mean throughput, linear regression and even
manually adjusting our predictions. However, all of them had their
drawbacks. This paper presents what we think will be the best approach
to forecast project deadline: Monte Carlo Simulation. We explain how it
works, how to apply it in a project and how you can benefit from using
it.
