Courtland
PY  - 2020
AB  - Understanding the processes followed by organizations is important to
ensure business outcomes are achieved in an optimal, efficient and
compliant manner. Process mining techniques rely on the existence of
structured event logs captured by process management systems. These
systems are not always employed and may not capture all process steps,
leaving out those that occur through emails and chat software or edits
to documents and knowledge-management systems.
Here we present an algorithm for the automated extraction of processes
from unstructured natural-language documents. Action and topic analysis
is used to generate an event log, from which process models are mined
using standard techniques. We show the algorithm is capable of
generating consistent software-development processes from an Apache
Camel email dataset.
