AU  - Marrella, Andrea
AU  - Montali, Marco
PY  - 2017
AB  - Process mining is an emerging area that synergically combines
model-based and data-oriented analysis techniques to obtain useful
insights on how business processes are executed within an organization.
This tutorial aims at providing an introduction to the key analysis
techniques in process mining that allow decision makers to discover
process models from data, compare expected and actual behaviors, and
enrich models with key information about the actual process executions.
In addition, the tutorial will present concrete tools and will provide
practical skills for applying process mining in a variety of application
domains, including the one of software development.
