AB  - Taking software project risk event as the study object, this paper
focuses on the problem of emergency disposal of software project risk
and Petri nets modeling method is introduced to analyze the concurrent
progresses. According to the happened risks, its emergency management
process is defined and its Petri nets model is built. Due to its
homogeneous characteristics with Markov chain, its Markov chain
constructed for above model. Through the analysis of activity,
accessibility, safety and other performances of the model to ensure its
availability and effectiveness. Quantitative analysis of the Markov
chain is carried on to explore the bottleneck factors that influence the
risk emergency process. The Petri nets modeling method provides a basis
for improving the rate of project risk emergency reaction process, and
ensures that the risks can be controlled just in time and software
project can be operated efficiently and safely.
