TI  - Towards an Approach to Support Software Process Simulation in Small and
Medium Enterprises
AU  - Silva Filho, Reinaldo Cabral
AU  - Cavalcanti da Rocha, Ana Regina
PY  - 2010
AB  - The use of software process simulation has been intensified in
enterprises and in academia. However, this reality does not apply to
small and medium sized software enterprises, given the lack of knowledge
on simulation, the absence of resources and the scarcity of historical
data of projects. This work presents the development of an approach to
facilitate software process simulation modelling in small and mid-sized
enterprises and describes an experience aimed at identifying weaknesses
and improvement opportunities to support the approach evolution. The
results of the experience pointed towards new research actions for the
development of the approach.
