TY  - CPAPER
TI  - Mining Software Process Lines
AU  - Rojas Blum, Fabian
PY  - 2016
AB  - There is a vast growth of generated event data being collected and
stored by organizations. Within the field of Process Mining, this data
has been used to discover, analyze and enhance processes from different
domains. For this purpose there are hundreds of techniques available in
different tools. These techniques are mostly focused on single
processes. On the other hand, there are several proposals for dealing
with multiple processes. Under different names, such as: configurable
process models, process families or process lines, processes are
characterized by capturing commonalities and variability between
(similar) process models. These approaches have shown to be useful for
organizations that have multiple variants of a given process, e.g.,
reducing redundancy and maintenance time. In this research proposal, we
are developing a framework that allows the use of Process Mining
techniques in families of processes within the software development
domain (i.e., Software Process Lines).
