AB  - This paper discusses the development of a set of object-oriented modular
simulation tools for solving lumped and spatially distributed models
generated from chemical process design and simulation problems.
Developed in the context of simulating semiconductor manufacture
equipment, this framework reduces the software development cycle time
associated with designing process systems and it improves the overall
efficiency of the simulator development process. Modularized simulator
components can be solved and analyzed individually, as well as formed
into modular systems that can be solved using sequential or simultaneous
approaches. A tungsten chemical vapor deposition simulation application
is presented to illustrate the capability of the proposed tools in
facilitating an evolutionary simulation approach. (c) 2006 Elsevier Ltd.
