PY  - 2015
AB  - Statistical usage testing (SUT) technique is the testing technique
defined it cleanroom software engineering. It based on developing the
usage models and then performing statistical tests on the usage models
(Runeson and Wohlin, IEEE Trans Softw Eng 20: 494-499, 1994). The
failure data from testing is then used in a software reliability model
to certify the reliability of the software. The main purpose of SUT is
to test a software product from a user's point of view. Hence, usage
models are designed and then test cases are developed from the models
(Prowell et al., Cleanroom software engineering technology and process,
1999). The paper tests Apache OpenOffice Writer using SUT Technique. The
paper makes use of two software RAM Commander and ITEM toolkit for
testing. In this paper, Markov chains are used to represent the usage
models. The development of Usage Markov Chain, the Testing Markov Chain
and incorporation of failure data is done using the same software. The
paper also discusses the analytical results of applying SUT and its
impact on software reliability.
