AB  - SimSWE is a library of components for modeling and simulation of
software engineering processes. It consists of a generic, implementation
independent description of the components and a reference implementation
using the MATLAB (R) / Simulink (R) environment. By providing
ready-to-use building blocks for typical functionality, the library
should facilitate and ease the use of simulation to analyze software
engineering issues. The goals are to provide a collection of reusable
components within an open and evolvable framework to help practitioners
develop simulation models faster and enable researchers to implement
complex modeling and simulation tasks. Currently, the library contains
more than thirty components. It can be used under the LPGL license. The
paper presents the current status of SimSWE to encourage its use and
participation within the research community.
