AU  - Deneckere, Rebecca
AU  - Hug, Charlotte
AU  - Salinesi, Camille
PY  - 2013
AB  - The paper addresses the problem of the low usage of software development
methods in software development practice. This has been recognized as
one of the key reasons for failures in software development projects and
a contributor to the low quality of software. We introduce a novel
approach that could help to improve the maturity of software development
processes. The approach is based on the method engineering principles
taking into account the limitations that hinder its use in practice. The
main objective of our research is to show that the method engineering
concepts are applicable in real settings and that could contribute to
the higher quality of software development processes and their products.
