TY  - JOUR
TI  - Automatically checking visual conformance for pushdown reactive systems
based on VPLs
AU  - Bonifacio, Adilson Luiz
PY  - 2026
AB  - Testing pushdown reactive systems is both an important and challenging
activity that guarantees a precise and robust software development
process. These systems are complex applications whose interaction with
the environment is regulated by a pushdown memory and, in general, can
be specified by the formalism of Input/Output Visibly Pushdown Labeled
Transition System (IOVPTS). Conformance checking, a model-based testing
technique, is used to verify whether an implementation under test (IUT)
complies with a given specification, using an appropriate conformance
relation. In this work, we establish a conformance relation based on
Visibly Pushdown Languages (VPLs) to model sets of desirable and
undesirable behaviors for such systems. We also show that complete test
suites can be generated using this new conformance relation over IOVPTS
models for pushdown reactive systems. Additionally, we implement an
automatic tool to check the proposed conformance relation and report
some experimental results.
