TI  - Agile Turn Guidance for Air-to-Air Missile with Linear Gauss
Pseudospectral Method
AU  - Gong, Xiaopeng
AU  - Zhang, Qian
AU  - Zhou, Hao
AU  - Chen, Wanchun
AU  - Qi,
Zhaohui
PY  - 2023
AB  - AN efficient three-dimensional agile turn guidance law for air-to-air
missiles is proposed, which is optimal, robust, and real-time. The
guided agile turn enables the missiles to improve the maneuverability
during mid-guidance phase to attack rear hemisphere targets in complex
combat scenarios. Based on the optimal trajectory solved by the
pseudospectral method, the solving procedure of the linear Gauss
pseudospectral (LGP) method to realize agile turn guidance is put
forward. The proposed guidance law generates the angle-of-attack and
sideslip angle commands in order to make the missile turn to a specified
direction in minimum time, as well as guarantees the robustness problem
due to the uncertainty of the aerodynamic coefficients after launching
at large off-axis angles. The results of Monte Carlo simulation indicate
that in practical situations, deviations of thrust, atmosphere density,
mass, and aerodynamic coefficient and target maneuver considered, the
angular deviation of the agile turn can satisfy accuracy requirement
through correction with LGP method. Furthermore, the computational
efficiency of the LGP program can satisfy the demands for onboard
application.
