System in Low Voltage Grid with Single-Phase Solar Power Generation
AU  - Puvi, Verner
AU  - Lehtonen, Matti
PY  - 2018
AB  - Modern electrical power system is evolving to a smarter and agile
system, which will support society's sustainable development. The low
voltage grid should be capable of withstanding new challenges such as
reverse power flows and voltage unbalance (VU) caused by distributed
generation. In this paper, the mitigation possibilities of the VU caused
by single-phase-connected photovoltaics (PV) are analysed with Tesla
Powerwall 2 battery energy storage systems (BESS) added to the grid.
Three different BESS phase connection strategies are modelled and the VU
is assessed with Monte Carlo Simulation (MCS). A low voltage
distribution grid in Sweden is considered with different PV and BESS
penetration levels and the applied method for VU assessment is
validated. Simulation results reveal the effectiveness of VU mitigation
by connecting PV and BESS to the same phase.
