TY  - CPAPER
TI  - Robust Next Release Problem: Handling Uncertainty During Optimization
AU  - Li, Lingbo
AU  - Harman, Mark
AU  - Letier, Emmanuel
AU  - Zhang, Yuanyuan
PY  - 2014
AB  - Uncertainty is inevitable in real world requirement engineering. It has
a significant impact on the feasibility of proposed solutions and thus
brings risks to the software release plan. This paper proposes a
multi-objective optimization technique, augmented with Monte-Carlo
Simulation, that optimizes requirement choices for the three objectives
of cost, revenue, and uncertainty. The paper reports the results of an
empirical study over four data sets derived from a single real world
data set. The results show that the robust optimal solutions obtained by
our approach are conservative compared to their corresponding optimal
solutions produced by traditional Multi-Objective Next Release Problem.
We obtain a robustness improvement of at least 18% at a small cost (a
maximum 0.0285 shift in the 2D Pareto-front in the unit space).
Surprisingly we found that, though a requirement's cost is correlated
with inclusion on the Pareto-front, a requirement's expected revenue is
not.
