AU  - Kroeninger, Kevin
AU  - Schulz, O.
PY  - 2015
AB  - The Bayesian Analysis Toolkit is a C++ package centered around
Markov-chain Monte Carlo sampling. It is used in high-energy physics
analyses by experimentalists and theorists alike. The software has
matured over the last few years. We present new features to enter
version 1.0, then summarize some of the software-engineering lessons
learned and give an outlook on future versions.
