AB  - Process discovery has been shown to be a challenging problem offering
limited results. This paper describes a new approach to process
discovery that examines the Internet information spaces of open source
software development projects. In particular, we examine challenges,
strengths, weaknesses and findings when seeking to discover, model, and
re-enact processes associated with large, global OSSD projects like
NetBeans.org. The longer-term goal of this approach is to determine the
requirements and design of more fully integrated process discovery and
modeling mechanisms that can be applied to Web-based, open source
software development projects.
