AB  - Process definition, verification, and validation are recognized as
critical elements in software process improvement, whereas CMMI is a
process improvement approach that provides organizations with the
essential elements of effective processes. Organizations must define
their own processes to meet the requirements of CMMI. A friendly,
unambiguous process modeling language and tool are thus very important
for organizations to define, verify, and validate the processes.
Nevertheless, hardly has any research yet been done on how to embed CMMI
process area goals into process definition stage to satisfy organization
