AB  - This paper describes the use of the BPM Method simulations for
estimating the appropriate number of resources in the software process
to balance its cost and duration. Extensions to the BPM Method that are
necessary to model the sharing and managing of limited resources are
defined and their conversion to the Petri Nets formalism is suggested to
specify the simulation semantics. Balancing formulas and ratios for
process cost and duration are provided and used for a local software
development company's software process simulations to find a balanced
number of workers in specific roles in the process.
