AB  - Organizations that develop software have recognized that software
process models are particularly useful for maintaining a high standard
of quality. In the last decade, simulations of software processes were
used in several settings and environments. This paper gives a short
overview of the benefits of software process simulation and describes
the development of a discrete-event model, a technique rarely used
before in that field. The model introduced in this paper captures the
behavior of a detailed code inspection process. It aims at reducing the
risks inherent in implementing inspection processes and techniques in
the overall development process. The determination of the underlying
cause-effect relations using data mining techniques and empirical data
is explained. Finally, the paper gives an outlook on our future work.
