PY  - 2006
AB  - This paper presents a value-based software process framework that has
been derived from the 4+1 theory of value-based software engineering
(VBSE). The value-based process framework integrates the four component
theories - dependency, utility, decision, and control, to the central
theory W, and orients itself as a 7-step process guide to practice
value-based software engineering. We also illustrate applying the
process framework to a supply chain organization through a case study
analysis.
