TY  - CPAPER
TI  - Software reliability assessment modeling based on nonlinear stochastic
differential equations of Ito type
AU  - Kimura, M
AU  - Yamada, S
AU  - Tanaka, H
PY  - 2000
AB  - This paper proposes a new software reliability assessment model which
describes nonlinear state dependency of software debugging processes.
Most of all software reliability growth models which have been proposed
up to the present treat the event of fault-detection in the testing and
operational phase of software development as a counting process. For
example, since NHPP (nonhomogeneous Poisson process) models for software
reliability assessment are discrete state space models, they cannot
describe the nonlinear state dependency of the software debugging
process without representing the nonlinearity in the mean value
functions of NHPP models. In order to model this nonlinearity as a
stochastic process itself, we propose a stochastic process model based
on a stochastic differential equation of Ito type, and derive several
quantitative measures for software reliability assessment. The
estimation method of unknown parameters is also presented.
