AB  - Software process simulation has been proposed as a means of studying
software development processes and answering specific questions about
them, such as, ``How feasible is a schedule?″ This study looked at
the question of schedule feasibility for a testing process constrained
by availability of test facilities. Simulation models of the testing
process were used to identify the significant factors affecting the test
