AB  - We propose a set of architectural patterns that describe a large variety
of neuro-symbolic systems. As in other areas of computer science
(knowledge engineering, software engineering, ontology engineering,
process mining and others), such design patterns provide a unified
vocabulary to describe a large variety of systems, help to systematise
the literature, clarify which combinations of techniques serve which
purposes, and encourage re-use of software components. We have validated
our set of compositional design patterns against a large body of recent
literature, and we apply them to a number of systems described in the
different sections of this volume.
Sections 1.1-1.7 of this chapter are based on our earlier publications
[1] and [2], the new contributions of this chapter are in section
1.5 and 1.6.
