TY  - CPAPER
TI  - Automated recognition of low-level process: A pilot validation study of
Zorro for test-driven development
AU  - Kou, Hongbing
AU  - Johnson, Philip M.
PY  - 2006
AB  - Zorro is a system designed to automatically determine whether a
developer is complying with the Test-Driven Development (TDD) process.
Automated recognition of TDD could benefit the software engineering
community in a variety of ways, from pedagogical aids to support the
learning of test-driven design, to support for more rigorous empirical
studies on the effectiveness of TDD in practice. This paper presents the
Zorro system and the results of a pilot validation study, which shows
that Zorro was able to recognize test-driven design episodes correctly
89% of the time. The results also indicate ways to improve Zorro's
classification accuracy further, and provide evidence for the
effectiveness of this approach to low-level software process
recognition.
