AB  - A new process for separating propylene and propane in ethylene
production has been put forward in which the extractive distillation
with aqueous acetonitrile (ACN) as entrainer is employed. A PRO/II
software process simulation has been made with the selection of an
appropriate vapor-liquid equilibrium model. The new process, extractive
distillation, requires a small number of trays, less energety
consumption and small column diameter. In the design of the distillation
column a new type of multi-overflow compound slant-hole tray was adopted
which has been widely used in the recent years. It is believed that with
the new process the industrial separation of propylene and propane is
greatly improved. (C) 2001 Elsevier Science B.V. All rights reserved.
