AB  - A generic, abstract model and the simulation shell based on it, both
called SUMMERS, are used as a framework for the implementation of
stochastic micropopulation models; in these, each individual is followed
separately while moving through a sequence of states. The shell supports
groups of interacting members, individual characteristics and multiple
simultaneous activities. Stochastic decisions may be made using Monte
