TY  - CPAPER
TI  - A stochastic model of human error during software development
AU  - Stutzke, M
AU  - Agarwal, M
AU  - Smidts, C
PY  - 1998
AB  - In order to gain insight into the nature of human errors that occur
during software development, a stochastic model has been developed that
relates the software failure intensity function to human error
occurrence throughout all software life cycle phases. The model
considers two broad categories of human error: (1) development error
made during design and coding activities and (2) debugging errors made
during attempts to remove faults identified during software inspections
and dynamic testing. The software development schedule and influencing
factors (e.g.,experience, schedule pressure, etc.) are used to predict
human error rates.
